---
import Layout from '../layouts/WC2026Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Rules" active="rules">
  <section>
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="label">Rules</h2>
      <span class="count">How it works</span>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <div>
        <h3 class="label">The draw</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>All 48 teams are sorted by FIFA rank and split into six strength tiers of eight.</li>
          <li>Each player receives exactly one team from every tier.</li>
          <li>No player holds two teams from the same group.</li>
          <li>The draw is randomised but optimised to keep total squad strength balanced.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="label">The scoring</h3>
        <p>
          Group stage: <strong>3</strong> points per win, <strong>1</strong> per draw (maximum 9 per team).
        </p>
        <p>
          Knockout progression bonuses, cumulative &mdash; a team keeps the points for every
          round it clears. The ladder <strong>doubles</strong> each round, so each stage is
          worth about as much as the entire run up to it:
        </p>
        <table class="scoring">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Reach the Round of 32 (qualified)</td><td><strong>5</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reach the Round of 16</td><td><strong>10</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reach the Quarter-final</td><td><strong>20</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reach the Semi-final</td><td><strong>40</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Win the third-place play-off <em>(beaten semi-finalists only)</em></td><td><strong>60</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reach the Final</td><td><strong>80</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Win the World Cup</td><td><strong>160</strong></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          The third-place play-off is the one step off the straight climb: a beaten
          semi-finalist who wins it banks <strong>60</strong> (their 40, plus 20),
          while the losing semi-finalist (fourth place) keeps 40.
        </p>
        <p>
          A player's score is the sum across their six teams of group points plus the
          deepest progression bonus reached. The table sorts by points, then goal
          difference, then goals for.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="fineprint">
        The ladder is weighted heavily towards progression: the 160-point champion bonus
        means the winner's owner finishes top of the table about 99.2% of the time. The
        rare exception goes to whoever has the broadest spread of deep runs across their
        six teams.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
